              "message": "Classification rules:  Business Area must be exactly one of: Corporate, Stock, Market, Economy.  Topic must be exactly one of: Regulatory, M&A, Risks, Strategy, Sales, Price Action, Technical Analysis, Legal, Appointment, Market, Financial, Dividend Policy, Coverage, Signal, Fundamentals, Reputation.  Sentiment must be exactly one of: Positive, Neutral, Negative.  Priority must be exactly one of: Low, Medium, High.  Priority rules: - High: material negative or risk-sensitive information requiring immediate analyst attention, especially severe Legal, Risks, Regulatory, earnings warning, fraud, major loss, or crisis events. - Medium: meaningful but non-urgent corporate or market developments such as M&A, regulatory approvals, strategic changes, notable earnings developments, or significant price movements. - Low: routine commentary, minor updates, or low-impact information.  Do not classify a positive regulatory approval as High priority unless the text clearly indicates an urgent material risk.  Summary must be one concise factual sentence. Do not provide investment advice. Follow the required structured output format exactly."
            }
